From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:17:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] usb: gadget: f_ncm: retry the timeout flush while u_ether
 is busy

The TX timer flushes the NTB that is still being filled by calling
ndo_start_xmit(NULL). When every IN request is still in flight, u_ether
answers NETDEV_TX_BUSY before it wraps the data, and the flush was
lost: the last NTB of a burst (up to 32 KiB) stayed queued until some
other packet came. On the Galaxy A22 5G this stalled SSH transfers for
tens of seconds.

The data is still held in ncm->skb_tx_data, so restart the timer and
try again a little later.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
index bf02545b3..b6d1ea545 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
@@ -1158,7 +1158,17 @@ static enum hrtimer_restart ncm_tx_timeout(struct hrtimer *data)
 		 *
 		 * This will call directly into u_ether's eth_start_xmit()
 		 */
-		netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev);
+		/* A22x: when every IN request is still in flight u_ether answers
+		 * NETDEV_TX_BUSY before wrapping, and the flush was lost: the last
+		 * NTB of a burst (up to 32 KiB) stayed queued until some other
+		 * packet came, which stalled SSH transfers for tens of seconds.
+		 * The data is still held here, so try again a little later.
+		 */
+		if (netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev) == NETDEV_TX_BUSY &&
+		    READ_ONCE(ncm->skb_tx_data)) {
+			hrtimer_forward_now(data, TX_TIMEOUT_NSECS);
+			return HRTIMER_RESTART;
+		}
 	}
 	return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 }
